<article class="env-definition" id="08WH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08WH">Definition <span data-tag="08WH">35.4.2</span>.</a> A <em>split equalizer</em> is a diagram (<a href="/tag/08WG" data-tag="08WG">35.4.1.1</a>) with $g_1 \circ f = g_2 \circ f$ for which there exist auxiliary morphisms $h : B \to A$ and $i : C \to B$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation" id="08WI">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/08WI" data-tag="08WI">35.4.2.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{descent-equation-split-equalizer-conditions} h \circ f = 1_ A, \quad f \circ h = i \circ g_1, \quad i \circ g_2 = 1_ B. \end{equation}</div>
</div>
</article>